# uboot-notools.config — disable U-Boot's host-side image-tooling (a PROVIDER default).
#
# These are NOT board facts and NOT a host workaround to route around — they're how we build
# U-Boot for this class of target: a sunxi image we FEL-load / `sf`-read raw, never sign, and
# never wrap for UEFI. So the signing/EFI host tools are dead weight. The uboot provider applies
# this unconditionally (recipe.sh), independent of board — hence it lives with the provider, not
# in a board.conf or the engine defaults.
#   TOOLS_LIBCRYPTO   host-side FIT/image SIGNING via libcrypto — we don't sign. (It also needs
#                     OpenSSL 1.1+; on an older host it wouldn't even build — but the reason to
#                     disable it is that we don't sign, not the host's openssl version.)
#   TOOLS_KWBIMAGE    Marvell Kirkwood image tool (selects TOOLS_LIBCRYPTO) — irrelevant to sunxi.
#   TOOLS_MKEFICAPSULE UEFI capsule update tool — no UEFI on this SD/NOR boot path.
# CONFIG_TOOLS_LIBCRYPTO is not set
# CONFIG_TOOLS_KWBIMAGE is not set
# CONFIG_TOOLS_MKEFICAPSULE is not set
